## 2. Check whether the missing NEG exists in Google Cloud

```
gcloud compute network-endpoint-groups list \
  --project=weather-project-prod-511603 \
  --filter="name:k8s1-c1bd0ffd-kube-system-default-http-backend-80-7739e04a"
```

If the service exists but the NEG is missing, we need to determine why GKE's controller expects that NEG before changing or recreating resources.

## 3. Check the cluster events

```
kubectl get events -n kube-system \
  --sort-by=.lastTimestamp
```

Look for errors involving `default-http-backend`, NEG creation, or the GKE Ingress controller.

Please share the output of Step 1 first. It will tell us whether the default backend Service is missing, has no endpoints, or has a NEG configuration that needs investigation. Don't delete your existing application Services or Ingress yet.